(Section)

Then He, glory be to Him, mentioned the reward of those who were saved from these trials by piety, which is the Gardens and the springs, and that they will be ﴿taking what their Lord has given them﴾ of goodness and honor.

In this there is evidence for several matters. Among them: their acceptance of it;

among them: their contentment with it;

among them: their reaching it without any hindrance or obstacle;

among them: that their reward is of the same kind as their deeds. For just as they took what He had commanded them in this world and met it with contentment, submission, and openness of heart, so they take what He has given them as reward.

Then He mentioned the cause that brought them to this, which is their ihsan (excellence in worship, glossed as doing what is good and beautiful), which entails worshipping Him alone with no partner and fulfilling His rights and the rights of His servants.

